 "recap": [
  "Two orders: subject first with ay, or predicate first (everyday).",
  "To flip: move the predicate to the front, delete ay, keep the marker with the subject.",
  "Ay links the subject to a description, an identity or an action.",
  "A flipped plural predicate takes mga: Mga bata sina Ana at Ben.",
  "At can shrink to 't after a vowel, and an obvious subject can be left out."
 ]
